# 4. PRODUCT DESIGN PRINCIPLE

The Phase 9 architecture must support:

```text
Tenant
   ↓
Organization
   ↓
Performance Configuration
   ↓
Performance Cycle
   ↓
Goals / KPIs / KRAs
   ↓
Employee Progress
   ↓
Self Assessment
   ↓
Manager Assessment
   ↓
Peer / 360 Feedback
   ↓
Calibration
   ↓
Final Review
   ↓
Approval
   ↓
Development Plan
   ↓
Training / Learning
   ↓
Promotion / Compensation Recommendation
   ↓
Analytics
```

Do not create isolated modules.

All modules must work together.

---

# 5. PERFORMANCE CYCLE MANAGEMENT

Create a configurable performance-cycle system.

Examples:

* Annual
* Half-yearly
* Quarterly
* Monthly
* Probation
* Custom cycle

A performance cycle should contain:

```text
Cycle ID
Tenant ID
Name
Description
Cycle Type
Start Date
End Date
Goal Start Date
Goal End Date
Self Review Start
Self Review End
Manager Review Start
Manager Review End
Peer Review Start
Peer Review End
Calibration Start
Calibration End
Finalization Date
Status
Created By
Created At
Updated At
```

Statuses:

```text
DRAFT
SCHEDULED
GOAL_SETTING
IN_PROGRESS
SELF_REVIEW
MANAGER_REVIEW
PEER_REVIEW
CALIBRATION
FINAL_REVIEW
COMPLETED
CANCELLED
ARCHIVED
```

Implement proper state transitions.

Do not allow invalid transitions.

---

# 6. PERFORMANCE CYCLE CONFIGURATION

HR/Admin should be able to configure:

* Cycle duration
* Review stages
* Rating scale
* Goal weightage
* Competency weightage
* Manager review weightage
* Self review weightage
* Peer review weightage
* 360 feedback
* Calibration
* Approval requirements
* Required comments
* Required goals
* Minimum number of goals
* Maximum number of goals
* Mandatory competencies
* Review visibility
* Notification schedule

Example:

```text
Goal Weight = 60%
Competency = 20%
Manager Review = 20%
```

Configuration must be tenant-specific.

