# 12. GOAL MILESTONES

Each goal can contain milestones.

Example:

```text
Goal
 ├── Milestone 1
 ├── Milestone 2
 ├── Milestone 3
 └── Final Target
```

Milestone fields:

```text
Title
Description
Due Date
Status
Progress
Completed Date
Owner
```

---

# 13. GOAL PROGRESS TRACKING

Employees should be able to update progress.

Support:

* Percentage progress
* Numeric progress
* Comments
* Evidence
* Attachments
* Milestones
* Achievement notes

Maintain historical progress records.

Do not overwrite historical progress.

Example:

```text
Goal Progress History

01-Jan → 10%
01-Feb → 25%
01-Mar → 40%
01-Apr → 65%
01-May → 90%
```

---

# 14. GOAL APPROVAL

Goals may require manager approval.

Workflow:

```text
DRAFT
 ↓
SUBMITTED
 ↓
MANAGER_REVIEW
 ↓
APPROVED / REJECTED
```

If rejected:

```text
Rejected
 ↓
Employee edits
 ↓
Resubmits
```

Reuse the existing approval engine from earlier phases where possible.

---

# 15. WEIGHTAGE MANAGEMENT

Implement configurable weightage.

Example:

```text
Goal 1 = 30%
Goal 2 = 20%
Goal 3 = 25%
Goal 4 = 25%

Total = 100%
```

Prevent invalid configurations.

Rules:

* Weight cannot be negative.
* Weight cannot exceed allowed limits.
* Total weight should satisfy configured rules.
* Finalized goals cannot be silently modified.

---

# 16. PERFORMANCE RATING SYSTEM

Create configurable rating scales.

Example:

```text
1 — Does Not Meet Expectations
2 — Partially Meets Expectations
3 — Meets Expectations
4 — Exceeds Expectations
5 — Outstanding
```

Allow tenants to configure:

* Rating name
* Score
* Description
* Minimum score
* Maximum score
* Rating color/display metadata
* Active/inactive

Do not hard-code ratings.

