# 119. CRITICAL DEVELOPMENT INSTRUCTION

Do NOT start by generating random files.

Follow this sequence:

```text
STEP 1
Inspect repository

↓

STEP 2
Understand existing architecture

↓

STEP 3
Map existing Phase 1–8 functionality

↓

STEP 4
Identify reusable services/components

↓

STEP 5
Design Phase 9 database changes

↓

STEP 6
Create migrations

↓

STEP 7
Implement backend domain/services

↓

STEP 8
Implement APIs

↓

STEP 9
Implement frontend

↓

STEP 10
Implement notifications/background jobs

↓

STEP 11
Implement reports/analytics

↓

STEP 12
Implement security

↓

STEP 13
Write automated tests

↓

STEP 14
Run complete regression suite

↓

STEP 15
Fix all failures

↓

STEP 16
Update documentation

↓

STEP 17
Provide final implementation report
```

---

# 120. MOST IMPORTANT RULE

**INSPECT FIRST → UNDERSTAND SECOND → DESIGN THIRD → IMPLEMENT FOURTH → TEST FIFTH → REPORT LAST**

Do not assume the repository structure.

Do not recreate existing modules.

Do not replace working code unnecessarily.

Do not break Phase 1–8 functionality.

Do not bypass existing:

* Authentication
* RBAC
* Tenant isolation
* Employee relationships
* Approval workflows
* Notification services
* Audit logging
* File storage
* Database conventions
* Frontend design system
* CI/CD

The objective is to make **AxonTimeHR Phase 9 production-ready, scalable, secure, maintainable, testable, and fully integrated with all previously completed phases.**

---

# END OF PHASE 9 DEVELOPMENT PROMPT

This phase gives AxonTimeHR a strong **core HR/performance layer** and also creates the foundation for later AI-driven HR analytics. A logical next phase would be **Phase 10 — Advanced HR Analytics, Workforce Planning, Recruitment/ATS & AI-powered HR Intelligence**.
